course: dictionary
lesson: 834
title: Many meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and context tells you which one to use. «Bend down» means lean your body down, but «bend the rules» means break them a little. Look at the words next to bend to find the right meaning.
explain: «In cricket the bowler keeps the arm straight; bending and straightening it to throw is against the rules.» Here bending the arm would break the rules, so bend means to make something curved, not straight. Ask yourself: does the sentence want a curve, a lean, or a rule broken?
explain: Bend can also be a noun. A bend is a curve in a road, river or pipe. «Bending down can be hard or painful for older people, so pick up what they drop.» Here bending means leaning your body down.
fact: Bend is a verb and a noun: to bend, bends, bent, bending; a bend, bends.
fact: To bend is to make something curved, not straight.
fact: To bend is to lean your body forward or down.
fact: A bend is a curve in a road, river or pipe.
fact: To bend the rules is to break them a little.
exercise: «Bending down can be hard or painful for older people, so pick up what they drop.» What does bending down mean here? | Breaking a rule | *Leaning your body down | Making a straight line | Walking around a corner
exercise: The road has a sharp bend near the river. What is a bend? | Water running fast over stones | A tall, straight tree | A broken rule | *A curve in a road, river or pipe
exercise: «In cricket the bowler keeps the arm straight; bending it to throw is against the rules.» What does bending the rules mean? | Reading the rules aloud | Writing new rules for the game | Making the rules bigger | *Breaking them a little
test: «A thinking trap is a habit of thought that bends the truth, making things seem worse than they are.» What does bends the truth mean? | Makes the truth straight and simple | *Twists the truth a little | Hides the truth under a rug | Tells the truth very loudly
test: Dad says, «Bend the wire into a circle.» What should you do to the wire? | Leave it straight | Cut it into small pieces | *Make it curved | Paint it red
exam: «Suleiman whispers: Little man, you know that all your stamping wouldn't bend one blade of grass.» In this sentence, what does bend mean? | Run over the grass quickly | Count every blade of grass | Cut the grass short | *Make something curved or change its shape
